R3/sonnet-1/m-8.text:
@priya.raman root cause confirmed. Impact: 0/132 streamroute hosts ROUTING; ledger cells lc-01..08 backlog 5.76M records, lag ~3,100 s (Kinesis retention 72h, so no data loss yet); canary failing; settlement-daily 12:30 gate at risk. Cause: os.limit_nproc=1024 per host; thread budget ~770 base + 2/peer + 8 build workers. At 120 hosts = 1016 (fits, barely); at 132 hosts (131 peers) = 1040 > 1024 -> shard-map build can't start workers (log: 'unable to create native thread'), maps expire, hosts BROKEN. Gossip took ~60 min to reach old hosts, hence errors from ~07:06, not at 06:41. NOT heap (xmx 2.2/6 GiB used, so RB-SR-04 is wrong) and NOT ledger-writer 3.41 (ledger CPU is idle because nothing arrives). 
Pacing per RB-SR-07: restart is useless until the cause is gone (step 1) - restarted hosts would hit the same 1024 limit, and a fleet_restart job can't be cancelled. OS limits can't be changed (PF §4.3). So the fix is to get back to 120 hosts (matches PLAT-2291 pre-state, tf drift says desired should be 120).
PROPOSED (class B, needs your APPROVED record, I'm executor): 1) ASG vl-streamroute-asg MinSize 132->120, DesiredCapacity 132->120 (NewestInstance policy terminates the 12 newest, sr-*-041..044 etc, which are the PLAT-2291 adds). Undo: set min/desired back to 132 (don't, until limits fix). 2) then per RB-SR-07: set /streamroute/prod/shardmap/bootstrap_source=authoritative (4.1(f), I'll record), fleet_restart batch_size 12, then revert to peers. Ok to approve 1?
